-- 0127 · رحلة الحريف في الصفحة الرئيسية — every word of the new sections, in the five languages.
--
-- Its test is supabase/tests/077_journey.sql (rolled back):
--   node --env-file=.env scripts/db-dry-run.mjs supabase/migrations/0127_journey.sql supabase/tests/077_journey.sql
--
-- THE OWNER'S REQUEST (2026-10-05, after approving the prototype): «ركّبهم في الصفحة الرئيسية مع النصوص في
-- الإعدادات وبالخمس لغات». The prototype held its words in a TypeScript module on purpose; this is the change
-- that moves them where the owner can reach them, and deletes that module.
--
-- FOUR LISTS AND NOT A HUNDRED KEYS. The sections repeat: eleven scenes, seven steps, ten questions, nine
-- example rows — 37 rows of two or three fields each. As individual settings that is ~100 keys and ~400
-- translation rows, and reordering a step would mean renumbering a dozen of them. They are stored the way
-- site.faq and site.quotes already are: one json setting per list, and one fully translated list per language
-- in public.translations, which is exactly what config.ts's settingValue() reads for a non-object value.
--
-- `key` AND `icon` INSIDE THE LISTS ARE NOT WORDS and must not be translated: the code looks the drawing up
-- by them (SCENE_VIEWS, GLYPHS). A translated `key` silently draws nothing. The description on each row says
-- so in the Back Office, where somebody editing the list will actually read it.

on conflict (key) do nothing;

on conflict (entity, entity_key, field, locale) do nothing;
